This repository is PUBLIC BUT NOT OPEN SOURCE.

It is public because the product requires it to be. Open Ledger Sports publishes
a SHA-256 commitment for every board before the games are played, and reveals
the full board afterwards, win or lose. That record is only worth something if
anyone can check it. Publishing the repository is how the claim is made
verifiable rather than merely asserted.

Publishing it is not a grant of rights to the code.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

  - Read anything here.
  - Verify anything here. Recompute the commitment hashes in
    data/commitments.json against the revealed boards, audit data/ledger.json,
    check that the published record matches what the code actually does. This
    is encouraged. It is the entire point.
  - Quote or cite it, with attribution, for commentary, journalism, teaching or
    research.
  - Fork it within GitHub. GitHub's Terms of Service grant that to every user of
    a public repository and this licence does not pretend to override them.
    Forking is not permission to USE what you forked beyond the above.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

  - Run this code, in whole or in part, to produce picks, predictions, ratings
    or odds analysis, for yourself or for anyone else.
  - Copy, adapt or translate any part of it into another project, including a
    reimplementation in another language that is derived from this source.
  - Redistribute it, host it, or offer it as a service.
  - Use it commercially in any form.

"Any part" includes the model in scripts/, the circuit-breaker logic, the
commit-and-reveal mechanism, the site templates, and the written content in
blog/ and the site copy.


THE DATA

data/ledger.json, data/commitments.json and the revealed boards are published as
a factual record for verification. Facts are not owned. You may cite the record,
check it, and report on it. You may not present it as your own, and you may not
use it to imply an endorsement, affiliation or partnership that does not exist.


